# Ownership boundaries for a three-person team.
#
# GitHub auto-requests a review from the owner of every path a PR touches. The
# point is not gatekeeping — it is that a PR crossing the frontend/backend
# boundary is *visibly* crossing it, and gets both pairs of eyes.
#
# Replace the placeholder handles below with real GitHub usernames before the
# first PR, or CODEOWNERS is silently inert.

# Default owner: anything not matched below.
*                       @Kartikkulk

# ── backend ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/apps/api/              @BACKEND-DEV
/contracts/             @BACKEND-DEV @FRONTEND-DEV

# ── frontend ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/apps/web/              @FRONTEND-DEV

# ── shared: integration owner reviews these ────────────────────────────────
/collectors/            @Kartikkulk
/Makefile               @Kartikkulk
